+      <section class="chapter" id="checklist" aria-labelledby="checklist-title">
+        <div class="chapter-head"><span class="number">11</span><div><h2 id="checklist-title">Review checklist</h2><p>This supports a review. Completing it does not automatically authorize a release.</p></div></div>
+        <ul class="checklist" id="review-checklist"><li><label><input type="checkbox"> <span>I selected study, param or bench and defined the question and metric units.</span></label></li><li><label><input type="checkbox"> <span>I checked synthetic versus recorded evidence, source identity and input completeness.</span></label></li><li><label><input type="checkbox"> <span>For a study, I retained the arms, seeds, shared input and comparison reference.</span></label></li><li><label><input type="checkbox"> <span>For History, I distinguished opportunities, acknowledged starts and verification, and inspected fallback.</span></label></li><li><label><input type="checkbox"> <span>For /bench, I reviewed the diff, test results and EXACT baseline fidelity.</span></label></li><li><label><input type="checkbox"> <span>I checked final status, usable ticks, missing data and exclusion reasons.</span></label></li><li><label><input type="checkbox"> <span>I did not equate changed choices with improvement, predicted cost with spend, or expected loss with a per-draw guarantee.</span></label></li><li><label><input type="checkbox"> <span>I retained input, reports and evidence; claims about real outcomes require appropriate real evidence.</span></label></li></ul>
+        <p class="checklist-progress" id="checklist-progress" role="status" aria-live="polite">0 of 8 items checked. Selections are not saved when you close the page.</p>
+        <div class="notice good"><strong>A useful result note looks like this:</strong>“On the specified baseline commit and N valid samples, the candidate with this diff passed the targeted tests. Baseline fidelity was EXACT. Metrics X and Y changed by these amounts; Z was unavailable or adverse. This is replay evidence. Acceptance still needs code review and appropriate live evaluation.”</div>
+      </section>
+
+      <section class="chapter" id="reference" aria-labelledby="reference-title">
+        <div class="chapter-head"><span class="number">12</span><div><h2 id="reference-title">Quick reference and FAQ</h2><p>Send control commands as separate messages.</p></div></div>
+        <div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Command</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>/study</code></td><td>Help for declarative JSON studies; attach a file to run.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/start</code> or <code>/help</code></td><td>Show bot usage to an authorized account</td></tr><tr><td><code>/check</code></td><td>Check prerequisites and service access</td></tr><tr><td><code>/guide</code></td><td>Download this English playbook as HTML and PDF attachments in the same chat</td></tr><tr><td><code>/upload</code></td><td>Instructions for code/parameter files and JSON studies</td></tr><tr><td><code>/templates</code></td><td>Download eight examples: five code/parameter files and three study JSON files</td></tr><tr><td><code>/validate</code></td><td>Use as a document caption to validate without running</td></tr><tr><td><code>/bench [options] &lt;description&gt;</code></td><td>Generate and test a code candidate; options precede the description</td></tr><tr><td><code>/param &lt;ID&gt; &lt;values...&gt; [options]</code></td><td>Compare parameter values with the recorded control</td></tr><tr><td><code>/status</code></td><td>Current execution stage and queue</td></tr><tr><td><code>/runs</code></td><td>The five most recent history records</td></tr><tr><td><code>/cancel</code></td><td>Request cancellation of the current job after its current step. Stopping may not be immediate.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/invite</code></td><td>Owner only, in private chat: a one-use member invitation valid for 24 hours</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
+        <div class="grid2"><div class="command"><div class="command-top"><span>See recent runs</span><button class="copy" type="button" data-copy="cmd-runs">Copy</button></div><pre><code id="cmd-runs">/runs</code></pre></div><div class="command"><div class="command-top"><span>Cancel the current job after its current step</span><button class="copy" type="button" data-copy="cmd-cancel">Copy</button></div><pre><code id="cmd-cancel">/cancel</code></pre></div></div>
+        <details class="faq"><summary>Does any Word document or long description become a benchmark?</summary><p>No. Use valid code/parameter sections or a versioned study JSON request. Unregistered algorithms require implementation.</p></details><details class="faq"><summary>Does a study run the production brain?</summary><p>A study runs reference algorithms on explicit inputs. Its report identifies mode=REFERENCE_STUDY and evidence type. Live outcome claims need suitable evidence.</p></details><details class="faq"><summary>How do I repeat a study?</summary><p>Reuse the same request, data, seeds and implementation. A server dataset can change; retain the frozen resolved-request.json from evidence.zip.</p></details><details class="faq"><summary>Does /validate guarantee study success?</summary><p>It checks structure, limits and supplied trace shape. Server dataset availability and evidence completeness are checked at execution. PASS can later lead to NEEDS_DATA or PARTIAL.</p></details><details class="faq"><summary>Does /validate compile code or run Go tests?</summary><div><p>No. The /validate attachment caption checks file structure, options, parameter IDs and value domains, without queuing an experiment. Send the file with an empty caption to execute it. Go tests and replay preflight apply to code/parameter workflows. Studies use their own schema and evidence checks.</p></div></details>
+        <details class="faq"><summary>Do bench and params in one file apply the values to the new code?</summary><div><p>Each section creates independent experiments with their own controls and reports, executed in file order. Parameter values are compared using the baseline replay binary. Testing a fixed candidate with parameter overrides requires a separate engineering workflow.</p></div></details>
+        <details class="faq"><summary>Why does the activity bar not show a percentage?</summary><div><p>Model, test, build and replay durations are not known in advance. The card shows the actual stage and elapsed time with an activity indicator, refreshing every eight seconds while running. It records the terminal state when work finishes, fails, is cancelled or is interrupted by a restart.</p></div></details>
+        <details class="faq" open><summary>Can I say “run the previous candidate again with 500 ticks”?</summary><div><p>Not through the current interface. Each /bench request is independent and the model regenerates a patch. Identical descriptions do not guarantee identical diffs. Compare the diff, baseline and data between runs. There is no /rerun command.</p></div></details>
+        <details class="faq"><summary>Can I describe the change entirely in Persian?</summary><div><p>You can write a Persian description, but include exact file paths, function names and English code identifiers. Context retrieval currently relies on ASCII identifiers. A fully Persian description may retrieve too little useful context. The technical English examples in this guide are a more reliable way to specify the request.</p></div></details>
+        <details class="faq"><summary>Will the bot update old tests when a formula changes?</summary><div><p>No. Existing _test.go files are immutable. The bot may add a new test file for a new helper; it does not rewrite old tests to make a change pass. Establish whether the new code is wrong or the intended product contract is changing. A contract and test change needs separate review. The bot reports the failure log and stops before benchmarking.</p></div></details>
+        <details class="faq"><summary>Do passing tests approve the entire brain and release?</summary><div><p>No. These targeted tests do not cover the full CI suite, every package, or live tests. Review the diff, evidence quality, relevant metrics, and live effects in proportion to the change.</p></div></details>
+        <details class="faq"><summary>Zero changed decisions: does that mean the formula has no effect?</summary><div><p>It only means the selected action set did not differ on this experiment's valid ticks. The changed path may not have been active, another gate may have determined the result, rankings may have stayed the same, or the sample may be uninformative. Inspect the diff and experiment context first.</p></div></details>
+        <details class="faq"><summary>How do I open the HTML report?</summary><div><p>Download the report from Telegram and open it in a browser. Use the CSV in Excel or a data tool; read the diff in a text editor. This guide is also a self-contained file and can be read offline.</p></div></details>
